                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd92df85-2fef-3ec1-8ac3-e57049f96ed3",
                                        "entry_id": "ae114a20-02ca-32c5-8107-3669c114c889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A feeling of long-lasting ire for another, sometimes to the point of hatred, over a perceived wrongdoing; bitterness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee5ff6cf-82be-4f3f-a067-6a122fabe76d",
                                                "sense_id": "fd92df85-2fef-3ec1-8ac3-e57049f96ed3",
                                                "text": "I could almost see the rancor in his eyes when he challenged me to a fight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cfc4740-1ae0-31c3-9595-6766c5884827",
                                        "entry_id": "ae114a20-02ca-32c5-8107-3669c114c889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rancidity, rankness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f805bb3b-7851-436f-85b0-c1b664c05d21",
                        "source_entry_id": "d63f5a52-2a25-3eda-a2ff-3517ee671c34",
                        "target_lang_word": "rancour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rancour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f42a93e2-f9d4-3d90-9410-9a99d4668035",
                                        "entry_id": "0fa5f30c-1d92-3930-b16d-b7df0a6ed27a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "British, Canada, and Australia spelling of rancor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "119b9d55-e99d-4b61-899e-738f75aa45cb",
                                                "sense_id": "f42a93e2-f9d4-3d90-9410-9a99d4668035",
                                                "text": "By some paradoxical evolution rancour and intolerance have been established in the vanguard of primitive Christianity. Mrs. Spoker, in common with many of the stricter disciples of righteousness, was as inclement in demeanour as she was cadaverous in aspect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d1b23d6-f786-4ef8-a094-690f1a48a3b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "d63f5a52-2a25-3eda-a2ff-3517ee671c34",
                        "target_lang_word": "rencor",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rencor",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac91a461-c779-322d-a287-29faca7a8b08",
                                        "entry_id": "8b3fa50c-1485-38a5-9d74-c7860a7b0a87",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sentimiento de hostilidad duradero y arraigado contra algo o alguien."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a4add35-2a4d-4abf-aa66-4070ca226723",
                                                "sense_id": "ac91a461-c779-322d-a287-29faca7a8b08",
                                                "text": "Contra el primero que es el pecado es la quinta petiçion que dize ‘E déxanos las debdas nuestras’; que quiere dezir los pecados, e añádesse ‘commo las dexamosnos a nuestros debdores’, es a saber, el grand rencor e la saña e el odio."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72b6cab9-4315-47f1-8b1a-64e5ee920a5c",
                                                "sense_id": "ac91a461-c779-322d-a287-29faca7a8b08",
                                                "text": "Y si dura todavía la impaciencia, das con mucha industria la culpa al compañero, sin atender que a ti misma eres insufrible. Pasado el rencor, te vuelves con astucia a hacerte virtuosa, dando documentos y refiriendo sentencias espirituales con sutileza de ingenio, sin enmendarte de tus pasados defectos."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
